-- title:
--   Bixby, Seymour: four excluded minors for $\mathrm{GF}(3)$
-- statement:
--   **The excluded minors for ternary matroids**, as the rung $S(3,4)$ of Challenge 2:
--
--   $$\text{for } q\in\{2,3\},\ \text{the class of } \mathrm{GF}(q)\text{-representable matroids has at most four excluded minors up to isomorphism.}$$
--
--   For $\mathrm{GF}(3)$ the four excluded minors are $U_{2,5}$, $U_{3,5}$, the Fano matroid $F_7$ and its dual $F_7^*$ (Bixby; Seymour); for $\mathrm{GF}(2)$ the single excluded minor $U_{2,4}$ is counted again by the same bound.
-- source:
--   R. E. Bixby, On Reid's characterization of the ternary matroids, JCTB 26 (1979), https://doi.org/10.1016/0095-8956(79)90056-X; P. D. Seymour, Matroid representation over GF(3), JCTB 26 (1979), https://doi.org/10.1016/0095-8956(79)90055-8; stated as Theorem 6.5.7 in J. Oxley, Matroid Theory, 2nd ed.

